following_english_context:
This Antipater was at the first called Antipas, according to his fathers name, who (as it is reported) was

made gouernour of all Idumaea by king Alexander and his wife: and afterwards made a league  
                         with the Arabians, Gazeans, and Ascalonites, corrupting them, and insinuating himselfe into their fauours by diuers great presents bestowed vpon them. This young Antipater considering with himselfe what Aristobulus power was, and fearing least some mischiefe might be fall him thorow the hatred the young king had conceiued against him, he communicated with certaine of  the greatest reckoning amongst the lewes, and secretly and cunningly incensed them against Aristobulus;

